        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.448,
            0.644,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": "We similarly find the distances DM and MA:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.353,
            0.477,
            0.649,
            0.502
          ],
          "content": "DM  = \\sqrt{2^2 + 5^2} = \\sqrt{29}   units",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.351,
            0.512,
            0.65,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{MA} = \\sqrt{6^{2} + 2^{2}} = \\sqrt{40}   units.",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.552,
            0.886,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": "In general, the distance between the points $( \\bar { x } _ { 1 } , y _ { 1 } )$ and $( x _ { 2 } , y _ { 2 } )$ is given by"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.375,
            0.579,
            0.621,
            0.608
          ],
          "content": "\\sqrt{ \\left( x_{2} - x_{1} \\right)^{2} + \\left( y_{2} - y_{1} \\right)^{2} }",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.618,
            0.568,
            0.638
          ],
          "content": "and is cal<u>culated as shown in Fig. 1.8.</u>"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
